solari-python is a source fork of Solari's Python SDK, as published on PyPI:

  solari-core 0.2.1, solari-desktop 0.2.0, solari-sandbox 0.2.1  (MIT)
  solari-browser 0.1.3                                           (Apache-2.0)
  https://getsolari.com

The first commit imports them unmodified; every later change is its own
commit. Files of solari-browser changed by this fork (Apache-2.0, section
4(b)): solari_browser/__init__.py and solari_browser/errors.py (new exports
and StaleObservationError). solari_browser/observe.py, observation.py and
observer.js are new files.

The fast observe/act layer comes from solari-reflex
(https://github.com/hitakshiA/solari-reflex, MIT), which adapts code and
design from these MIT-licensed projects:

browser-use/jev-ultrafast — https://github.com/browser-use/jev-ultrafast
  packages/solari_browser/solari_browser/observer.js (the solari-reflex page
  observer) adapts jev_ultrafast/snapshot.js: accessible names, roles, the
  page key and per-control guards, and settling after an action.
  Copyright (c) 2026 Browser Use.

trycua/cua — https://github.com/trycua/cua
  packages/solari_core/solari_core/reflexd/reflexd.py follows cua-driver's
  accessibility-tree observation rules (only the active window and open
  popups, huge tables never enumerated), and observer.js borrows an unnamed
  row's or cell's own text as its label (PR #3914).
  Copyright (c) 2025 Cua AI, Inc.

The MIT license text for each is in its repository.
